1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,610
He wanted to have
a ritual performed with you

2
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:03,590
to help him get ahead in his career.

3
00:00:05,430 --> 00:00:07,630
I have a really bad feeling about this.

4
00:00:07,650 --> 00:00:09,800
You want to get close to him
for the case, right?

5
00:00:09,810 --> 00:00:11,880
There's nothing
to investigate about him.

6
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:13,310
You think something's off
about Mungkorn, too, right?

7
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,350
It's like...

8
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:15,790
He's under some kind of spell, right?

9
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:17,350
If he gets to sleep
with Mungkorn tonight,

10
00:00:17,370 --> 00:00:18,670
I don't think
things will end well for Mungkorn.

11
00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:19,500
I win.

12
00:00:19,530 --> 00:00:22,130
I'll try to make him remember
one more time.

13
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,850
- Mungkorn, don't leave.
- Saming, I want to go home.

14
00:00:25,870 --> 00:00:29,900
♪And all I want is
for it to belong to you♪

15
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:32,310
Ladies and gentlemen, meet...

16
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:34,890
Pol.Snr.Sgt.Maj. Mungkorn Phianwanich.

17
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:39,130
He is my husband.

18
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:43,200
We have been legally married

19
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:44,400
for a while now.

20
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:47,870
Since when were they married?

21
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:54,190
I'd like to ask you to wish us

22
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,820
a happy life together
with nothing standing in our way.

23
00:00:58,510 --> 00:01:00,980
May you all be witnesses to our promise

24
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:02,220
to love

25
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:04,210
and cherish each other forever.

26
00:01:05,430 --> 00:01:07,860
And no one will ever come between us

27
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:10,720
or tear us apart.

28
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:24,860
(Mungkorn will be freed
from the love spell)

29
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:29,670
(when you give him a heartfelt kiss
in front of everyone)

30
00:01:29,690 --> 00:01:32,140
(and declare your love for him)

31
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:34,170
(for all to hear.)

32
00:01:35,810 --> 00:01:38,890
It's like a sudden,
chaotic electrical surge, My Lady!

33
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:05,280
Thear.

34
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:09,990
You're back, aren't you?

35
00:02:22,010 --> 00:02:23,430
That's more like it.

36
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:52,160
Hold it right there.

37
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,870
Why the hell are you in my way?
Get lost!

38
00:02:53,890 --> 00:02:54,680
Here's the warrant.

39
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:59,420
Inspector Saming, you're under arrest.

40
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:00,930
What am I being charged with?

41
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:04,590
"Distribution, possession
with intent to distribute,

42
00:03:04,620 --> 00:03:08,270
and/or illegal consumption
of Category 1 narcotics."

43
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:12,190
We already know

44
00:03:12,210 --> 00:03:14,150
that you're the leader
of the Black Bull.

45
00:03:15,150 --> 00:03:16,440
What evidence do you have?

46
00:03:17,090 --> 00:03:18,500
You'd better not try to frame me.

47
00:03:18,710 --> 00:03:20,310
It came straight from your house.

48
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:29,810
Phuwin.

49
00:03:30,940 --> 00:03:31,860
- Huh?
- These teeth.

50
00:03:34,770 --> 00:03:36,570
Great, now we have more evidence.

51
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:38,560
Let me take a photo of them.

52
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,780
(Mungkorn left this notebook for you.)

53
00:03:45,610 --> 00:03:48,480
(Inspector Saming was spying on us
through the gifts he gave Mungkorn.)

54
00:03:48,510 --> 00:03:50,590
(And we've suspected him of being
involved with the dealer)

55
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:53,250
(who died from the poison hidden
in his teeth in the interrogation room.)

56
00:04:01,930 --> 00:04:02,810
Sh*t,

57
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:04,170
what's wrong with him?

58
00:04:27,790 --> 00:04:29,120
- Sergeant, take him away.
- This way, sir.

59
00:04:30,930 --> 00:04:31,670
Let's go.

60
00:04:33,270 --> 00:04:34,170
Don't touch me.

61
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:35,700
I can walk on my own.

62
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:47,750
Are you okay?

63
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:50,420
Let's sit here
and get some fresh air for a bit.

64
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:54,960
What have I done these past few days?

65
00:04:56,790 --> 00:04:59,560
I barely remember anything.

66
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,270
It's better that you don't.

67
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:08,770
I really don't want you
to remember any of it.

68
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:11,900
Because you were so mean to your lover.

69
00:05:16,830 --> 00:05:17,560
"Lover"?

70
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:22,400
So you consider yourself my lover now?

71
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:25,620
I am, from now on.

72
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:27,930
We're official now, after all.

73
00:05:38,230 --> 00:05:39,130
I...

74
00:05:39,870 --> 00:05:43,070
really thought I was going to lose you
to a terrible person like Saming.

75
00:05:47,110 --> 00:05:48,110
Thank you

76
00:05:48,990 --> 00:05:50,300
for not letting me go.

77
00:05:53,750 --> 00:05:56,470
A life where you're forced
to love someone like that...

78
00:05:59,580 --> 00:06:01,270
must be incredibly tragic.

79
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:08,880
And what about with me?

80
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:12,800
Do you feel forced, too?

81
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:15,580
At first, I did.

82
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:21,080
But not anymore.

83
00:06:21,430 --> 00:06:22,500
I'm here because I want to be.

84
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:43,030
How are you feeling?
Are you okay?

85
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:45,840
I don't think the curse
has completely worn off yet.

86
00:06:46,350 --> 00:06:49,350
Probably because I'm trying so hard
to remember what happened.

87
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:54,730
I think we should head inside
and get some rest. Come on.

88
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:55,590
Okay.

89
00:06:56,610 --> 00:06:57,390
Hey!

90
00:06:58,370 --> 00:06:59,530
I just thought of something better.

91
00:07:00,860 --> 00:07:02,570
I think you need to freshen up.

92
00:07:03,580 --> 00:07:04,700
How?

93
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:08,140
- Like this!
- Hey, you!

94
00:07:11,890 --> 00:07:12,870
What are you doing?

95
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:16,690
No!

96
00:07:16,710 --> 00:07:18,410
Come on, you need to freshen up!

97
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:20,530
- Stop it! Hey!
- In you go, Mungkorn!

98
00:07:29,910 --> 00:07:32,740
Thear, what is wrong with you?

99
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:34,260
So?

100
00:07:34,590 --> 00:07:35,650
Feeling refreshed now?

101
00:07:37,170 --> 00:07:38,830
Stop trying to remember the past.

102
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:41,580
Let's focus on making
new memories together instead.

103
00:07:43,490 --> 00:07:46,260
I have some vague memories, actually.

104
00:07:47,930 --> 00:07:49,270
I remember the touch.

105
00:07:50,690 --> 00:07:51,770
I remember the scent...

106
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:55,240
of the person I rode with
when I left Saming's house.

107
00:07:56,630 --> 00:07:57,770
What did it smell like?

108
00:08:01,250 --> 00:08:03,160
It was the scent that made me feel...

109
00:08:05,740 --> 00:08:06,980
safe.

110
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:28,200
See?

111
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:30,340
No matter what happens,

112
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:32,840
I'll always be in your heart.

113
00:08:33,570 --> 00:08:35,180
Nothing can ever take that away.

114
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:38,780
Don't get too ahead of yourself.

115
00:08:39,670 --> 00:08:41,580
If you keep acting like a jerk,

116
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:43,860
I'm really leaving for good.

117
00:08:47,050 --> 00:08:47,960
Wait, wait.

118
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,730
Stay and dance with me.

119
00:08:52,270 --> 00:08:53,670
In the pool? Seriously?

120
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:54,490
Of course.

121
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:58,600
To celebrate having
you back in my arms again.

122
00:08:58,990 --> 00:09:03,260
♪All I want when our hearts
finally intertwine♪

123
00:09:03,290 --> 00:09:08,440
♪Is for you to keep
the promise you made that time♪

124
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:12,960
♪Take care of my heart
and make me feel divine,♪

125
00:09:12,990 --> 00:09:21,110
♪Make all my dreams come true
with your love that's mine♪

126
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:41,650
From now on,

127
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:45,220
we're going public for everyone to see.

128
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:49,100
I've been waiting for
this day for a long time.

129
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:17,660
(Yin as Theartha)

130
00:10:22,630 --> 00:10:25,320
(War as Mungkorn)

131
00:10:29,470 --> 00:10:31,330
(Shane as Phuwin)

132
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:35,140
(Boss as Lukplub)

133
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:39,330
(Kit as Kanin)

134
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:41,170
(Tang as Nadol)

135
00:10:46,310 --> 00:10:50,180
(Tae as Saming)

136
00:11:34,420 --> 00:11:36,040
Why are you all over me so early?

137
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:37,840
What do you want?

138
00:11:40,150 --> 00:11:41,570
I don't really want anything.

139
00:11:46,950 --> 00:11:49,460
I just want to wake up to
a beautiful view like this forever.

140
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:52,740
You're the best view
in all of Northern Thailand.

141
00:11:54,150 --> 00:11:55,750
There you go, exaggerating again.

142
00:11:57,700 --> 00:11:58,830
I'm not exaggerating.

143
00:11:59,640 --> 00:12:01,260
A view this good...

144
00:12:03,150 --> 00:12:04,570
I want it all to myself.

145
00:12:05,370 --> 00:12:06,580
I'm not sharing it with anyone.

146
00:12:09,510 --> 00:12:10,580
See this part right here?

147
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:14,070
It's like a mountain range.

148
00:12:15,850 --> 00:12:18,660
As you drive up, see?

149
00:12:19,550 --> 00:12:22,950
It's a bumpy ride
because you have to cross so many peaks.

150
00:12:24,010 --> 00:12:25,350
At least five or six of them.

151
00:12:26,710 --> 00:12:27,690
But it's okay.

152
00:12:27,910 --> 00:12:29,380
I've always loved
a bit of an adventure anyway.

153
00:12:31,410 --> 00:12:33,360
Once you cross
the mountains to this point...

154
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:36,400
you reach the viewpoint
of these two peaks.

155
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:38,860
Drive carefully then.

156
00:12:39,150 --> 00:12:40,760
Watch out,
or you might fall off a cliff.

157
00:12:42,570 --> 00:12:44,350
Once I've made it this far...

158
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:45,960
I'm not afraid of anything anymore.

159
00:12:47,590 --> 00:12:50,390
Now I must decide which one to visit.

160
00:12:51,780 --> 00:12:53,450
The left one?

161
00:12:54,710 --> 00:12:56,550
But if I go for the left...

162
00:12:57,250 --> 00:12:59,150
the right one might get lonely.

163
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:05,020
Help me choose. What should I do?

164
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:06,770
I guess I'll just have to visit both.

165
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:07,840
Let's start with this one.

166
00:13:09,050 --> 00:13:09,930
Thear.

167
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:12,020
Wasn't last night enough for you? Huh?

168
00:13:12,730 --> 00:13:13,880
Alright, finished with this peak.

169
00:13:13,910 --> 00:13:15,080
Now onto the next one.

170
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:19,210
Stop it.

171
00:13:19,490 --> 00:13:20,580
That tickles!

172
00:13:22,770 --> 00:13:25,230
There's no such thing
as "enough" for me.

173
00:13:26,130 --> 00:13:27,130
You know...

174
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:29,910
simple things like this

175
00:13:30,290 --> 00:13:32,160
are exactly what I've wanted
to do for a long time.

176
00:13:33,050 --> 00:13:34,520
Married life...

177
00:13:35,430 --> 00:13:36,970
Waking up next to each other,

178
00:13:37,350 --> 00:13:38,890
cuddling in bed,

179
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:41,100
sharing meals, and showering together.

180
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,750
None of it is inherently special.

181
00:13:44,330 --> 00:13:45,490
It's the person who makes it special.

182
00:13:49,150 --> 00:13:50,110
And do you know...

183
00:13:50,550 --> 00:13:54,950
that I've wanted to be
a good partner for a long time, too?

184
00:13:59,570 --> 00:14:00,480
In what way?

185
00:14:01,730 --> 00:14:02,640
Well...

186
00:14:04,430 --> 00:14:06,960
by taking the best care of you.

187
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:09,240
Both at the dinner table...

188
00:14:10,570 --> 00:14:11,650
and in bed.

189
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:15,420
Well, we're in bed right now.

190
00:14:15,670 --> 00:14:16,780
So take care of me. Come here.

191
00:14:18,630 --> 00:14:20,100
And how exactly should you
"take care" of me in bed?

192
00:14:20,490 --> 00:14:22,520
Should we save that
for when we get home?

193
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:24,180
No point paying for extra time here.

194
00:14:24,940 --> 00:14:28,500
Oh, come on! We're already in bed!

195
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:29,650
Take care of me.

196
00:14:32,270 --> 00:14:33,070
Tell you what.

197
00:14:33,590 --> 00:14:35,790
Let's have breakfast at the hotel first.

198
00:14:35,910 --> 00:14:37,770
Then once we're back home,

199
00:14:38,210 --> 00:14:39,700
I'll cook for you.

200
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:42,860
We'll go grocery shopping
at the market together.

201
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:43,830
How does that sound?

202
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:45,630
But I'm hungry right now.

203
00:14:45,650 --> 00:14:46,740
What should we do?

204
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,190
Well...

205
00:14:48,810 --> 00:14:50,230
then let me have a bite of you.

206
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:54,970
- Wasn't last night enough?
- Not even close.

207
00:14:57,780 --> 00:14:58,440
So kissy.

208
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:15,720
Want some fries?

209
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,390
Is it good, Phuwin?

210
00:15:23,570 --> 00:15:25,860
Anything you feed me tastes delicious.

211
00:15:26,670 --> 00:15:27,890
Whoa, Phuwin.

212
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:30,170
You're being so sweet.
Guess you need no sugar in your coffee.

213
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:32,280
Well, I never add sugar anyway

214
00:15:32,310 --> 00:15:35,640
because Lukplub provides
all the sweetness I need.

215
00:15:36,020 --> 00:15:37,750
Someone with no love life like you...

216
00:15:37,930 --> 00:15:38,930
probably wouldn't understand.

217
00:15:39,330 --> 00:15:40,190
I do have someone.

218
00:15:41,820 --> 00:15:43,490
Look, he's walking over now.

219
00:15:47,190 --> 00:15:47,970
Whoa.

220
00:15:48,110 --> 00:15:48,840
- What's with you?
- Good morning.

221
00:15:48,870 --> 00:15:49,570
Good morning.

222
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:51,380
Mind if I join you?

223
00:15:51,410 --> 00:15:52,260
Please, take a seat.

224
00:15:52,290 --> 00:15:53,310
Go ahead.

225
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:54,720
Feel free.

226
00:15:56,940 --> 00:15:58,630
- Want some salad?
- Sure.

227
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:02,240
Is it good?

228
00:16:04,170 --> 00:16:06,000
And how's Mungkorn doing?

229
00:16:06,530 --> 00:16:07,970
Isn't he coming down for breakfast?

230
00:16:10,930 --> 00:16:12,070
Inspector Thear said

231
00:16:12,100 --> 00:16:13,620
he's still not feeling very well.

232
00:16:13,650 --> 00:16:15,140
So he wanted him to get some more rest.

233
00:16:17,290 --> 00:16:18,880
Resting, my ass.

234
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:22,030
That bastard is probably busy
"checking on Mungkorn" by now.

235
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:29,930
When are you going to
let me take care of you?

236
00:16:31,810 --> 00:16:34,340
I think I can handle myself just fine.

237
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:56,460
Give it to me.

238
00:16:56,490 --> 00:16:57,520
- Come on.
- Hey...

239
00:16:57,550 --> 00:16:58,450
Let me peel it for you.

240
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:29,370
I think I finally understand

241
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:31,750
why you were so annoyed with us.

242
00:17:33,950 --> 00:17:35,500
I don't like being challenged.

243
00:17:38,630 --> 00:17:41,310
Anyway, I'm rooting for both of you.

244
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:43,380
Both the one
who wants to care for the other...

245
00:17:44,070 --> 00:17:46,320
and the one who wants to be cared for.

246
00:17:48,660 --> 00:17:49,560
Would you like some coffee?

247
00:18:05,070 --> 00:18:06,460
Everything is all set.

248
00:18:06,490 --> 00:18:09,150
Thank you for letting us be part
of your special moment.

249
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:11,080
Congratulations to you both.

250
00:18:11,180 --> 00:18:13,920
Inspector Theartha and Sergeant Mungkorn

251
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:16,940
are now husband and husband.

252
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:19,100
Whoa, how do you know about us?

253
00:18:19,290 --> 00:18:20,600
Well,

254
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:22,760
with you announcing it
that loudly in the ballroom...

255
00:18:22,780 --> 00:18:24,280
how could anyone not know?

256
00:18:25,300 --> 00:18:28,040
Please come back and stay with us again.

257
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:28,960
Thank you.

258
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:30,440
- Yes, thank you so much.
- Thank you.

259
00:18:35,950 --> 00:18:36,880
What are you smiling about?

260
00:18:39,100 --> 00:18:40,940
I don't know. I'm just blushing.

261
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:45,260
It feels so heartwarming
when people call us that.

262
00:18:46,110 --> 00:18:47,810
It's like the first time

263
00:18:47,830 --> 00:18:50,510
I've truly felt like I'm your husband.

264
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:52,650
Is it really that much?

265
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:54,260
Alright then.

266
00:18:54,290 --> 00:18:57,330
From now on,
I'll be the one bragging about you.

267
00:18:57,560 --> 00:18:59,380
Seriously, with a husband this cute,
how could I not show you off?

268
00:18:59,410 --> 00:19:01,190
- In what way?
- Perfect timing! Hey, you!

269
00:19:01,220 --> 00:19:02,310
- Going somewhere?
- Yes?

270
00:19:02,530 --> 00:19:04,330
- I'm going to see my partner.
- Can you talk to me for a second?

271
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:05,920
- Sure.
- This is my husband.

272
00:19:05,940 --> 00:19:07,250
His name is Mungkorn.

273
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:07,960
Right.

274
00:19:07,980 --> 00:19:08,990
My mom forced us to get married.

275
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:10,540
At first, we weren't actually in love.

276
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:13,020
But as time went by,
we truly fell for each other.

277
00:19:13,130 --> 00:19:15,880
And now, I'm going to love him
until the day I die.

278
00:19:16,010 --> 00:19:17,960
- Heck, if he dies, I'm going with him.
- That's enough.

279
00:19:17,980 --> 00:19:19,760
We're both cops. Cool, right?

280
00:19:19,790 --> 00:19:20,620
Very cool.

281
00:19:20,650 --> 00:19:21,460
Yeah?

282
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:23,790
But wait, there's more! Listen.

283
00:19:23,810 --> 00:19:26,110
We used to fight like crazy.
There were so many obstacles.

284
00:19:26,130 --> 00:19:27,580
But we just made up yesterday.

285
00:19:27,730 --> 00:19:30,460
Now that we're good,
I decided to go all out.

286
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:31,860
Ugh, enough already!

287
00:19:32,190 --> 00:19:33,750
Why are you telling him that much?

288
00:19:33,770 --> 00:19:35,180
He probably knows
everything about us by now.

289
00:19:36,510 --> 00:19:38,550
I'm sorry on behalf of my husband.

290
00:19:38,580 --> 00:19:39,880
He's just a little overexcited.

291
00:19:39,910 --> 00:19:40,840
It's quite alright.

292
00:19:40,860 --> 00:19:41,950
My apologies.

293
00:19:42,220 --> 00:19:43,970
Go crazy again tonight, okay?

294
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:44,710
Wait...

295
00:19:44,740 --> 00:19:46,540
- Looks like you like it!
- Ugh!

296
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:47,640
Let's go home.

297
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,860
Hey, you and your partner
can have a chat with me later.

298
00:19:51,770 --> 00:19:56,670
(3 days later, Chiang Mai)

299
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:01,420
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

300
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:03,920
Believe it or not,

301
00:20:04,150 --> 00:20:05,780
I've never shopped at a market before.

302
00:20:06,570 --> 00:20:07,760
I can understand that.

303
00:20:08,070 --> 00:20:11,550
You grew up like a young master,
with everyone doing everything for you.

304
00:20:11,570 --> 00:20:13,260
Well, that's all changing now,

305
00:20:13,290 --> 00:20:14,440
ever since I have you.

306
00:20:20,110 --> 00:20:22,070
Half a kilo of bacon, please.

307
00:20:22,090 --> 00:20:22,970
Okay, dear.

308
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:26,050
I'm thinking of learning
a new style of cooking.

309
00:20:26,650 --> 00:20:27,900
Just to take a break from Northern food.

310
00:20:29,430 --> 00:20:31,440
I can eat it all the time.
I'll never get bored of it.

311
00:20:32,730 --> 00:20:34,550
Let me do something nice for my husband.

312
00:20:36,320 --> 00:20:39,070
But I don't know
if you'll like it or not.

313
00:20:40,660 --> 00:20:41,530
I don't mind.

314
00:20:42,320 --> 00:20:45,860
As long as you're the one cooking,
I'll eat anything.

315
00:20:46,750 --> 00:20:47,950
We'll see about that.

316
00:20:48,820 --> 00:20:50,380
- All set?
- Yes.

317
00:20:51,350 --> 00:20:53,420
- Thank you.
- Let me carry those. Come here.

318
00:20:53,790 --> 00:20:54,710
Here you go.

319
00:20:54,740 --> 00:20:55,600
Thank you, dear.

320
00:20:55,630 --> 00:20:56,670
Thank you.

321
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:08,570
Wow.

322
00:21:11,220 --> 00:21:12,710
That roti looks so delicious.

323
00:21:13,770 --> 00:21:15,130
But judging by the crowd...

324
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:17,730
it'll probably take half an hour.

325
00:21:20,060 --> 00:21:22,030
Want some? I'll wait in line for you.

326
00:21:22,930 --> 00:21:23,920
It's okay.

327
00:21:24,090 --> 00:21:25,370
I'd rather stand and wait with you.

328
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:28,050
It's fine. I'll queue up myself.

329
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:29,640
You go put the groceries in the car.

330
00:21:29,820 --> 00:21:31,330
Turn on the AC
and stay cool while you wait.

331
00:21:31,350 --> 00:21:32,420
I'll buy it for you.

332
00:21:32,650 --> 00:21:34,170
- You sure?
- Yeah.

333
00:21:35,430 --> 00:21:36,420
Thank you.

334
00:22:08,690 --> 00:22:09,850
Hello, Uncle.

335
00:22:10,430 --> 00:22:11,530
Is something wrong?

336
00:22:12,130 --> 00:22:13,970
Saming was released.

337
00:22:13,990 --> 00:22:15,060
Just this morning.

338
00:22:15,890 --> 00:22:17,080
How is that even possible?

339
00:22:17,110 --> 00:22:19,480
I thought I'd gathered solid evidence.

340
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:21,970
The prosecutor said
the evidence was insufficient.

341
00:22:22,030 --> 00:22:23,580
So he was released.

342
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:27,350
I don't know where he's planning to go
or what his next move is.

343
00:22:27,690 --> 00:22:31,070
But one thing's for sure,
he's probably furious with you two.

344
00:22:31,210 --> 00:22:32,340
Understood, Uncle.

345
00:22:33,540 --> 00:22:34,540
Thank you so much.

346
00:22:42,140 --> 00:22:43,870
- Can I order now?
- Certainly.

347
00:22:43,890 --> 00:22:46,540
Two with egg
and extra condensed milk, please.

348
00:22:59,380 --> 00:23:06,490
(TD 54006 Chiang Mai)

349
00:23:07,250 --> 00:23:08,670
- Hey, kid. Let me help.
- What a mess.

350
00:23:09,120 --> 00:23:09,860
There you go.

351
00:23:10,420 --> 00:23:11,110
It's okay, bro.

352
00:23:11,130 --> 00:23:13,200
Come on, I'll help
before you drop anything else.

353
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:14,720
Thank you.

354
00:23:14,740 --> 00:23:16,710
Don't mention it.
I work here at the market.

355
00:23:18,470 --> 00:23:19,880
Thank you so much.

356
00:23:21,560 --> 00:23:22,180
It's so hot...

357
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:49,970
(TD 54006 Chiang Mai)

358
00:23:52,010 --> 00:23:52,910
Mungkorn!

359
00:23:53,110 --> 00:23:54,330
Mungkorn! Mungkorn!

360
00:23:57,850 --> 00:23:58,890
Mungkorn!

361
00:24:00,530 --> 00:24:01,500
Mungkorn!

362
00:24:03,750 --> 00:24:04,730
Mungkorn!

363
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:13,250
(TD 54006 Chiang Mai)

364
00:24:13,280 --> 00:24:14,280
Mungkorn!

365
00:24:20,230 --> 00:24:22,620
(TD 54006 Chiang Mai)

366
00:24:22,640 --> 00:24:23,480
Sh*t!

367
00:24:40,260 --> 00:24:41,550
How's it going, old friend?

368
00:24:42,030 --> 00:24:42,990
Saming!

369
00:24:43,780 --> 00:24:44,940
What did you do to Mungkorn?

370
00:24:45,130 --> 00:24:46,350
Chill out.

371
00:24:46,870 --> 00:24:48,490
I haven't even done anything yet.

372
00:24:48,610 --> 00:24:50,740
But if you don't do exactly as I say...

373
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:54,460
I'll chop off
Mungkorn's fingers one by one.

374
00:24:55,100 --> 00:24:57,080
Until there isn't a single finger left
for your ring.

375
00:24:57,100 --> 00:25:00,030
Hey, you bastard!
Don't you dare touch him!

376
00:25:00,310 --> 00:25:01,640
Just take it out on me.

377
00:25:01,820 --> 00:25:02,950
Don't worry. I will.

378
00:25:03,700 --> 00:25:05,700
Come see me. I'll send you the address.

379
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:08,440
Don't tell anyone about this,

380
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:11,440
or Mungkorn won't leave in one piece.

381
00:25:11,940 --> 00:25:13,830
Hey, wait! Listen to me!

382
00:25:13,910 --> 00:25:14,710
Hey!

383
00:25:23,560 --> 00:25:26,160
(TD 54006 Chiang Mai)

384
00:25:28,530 --> 00:25:33,110
(TD 54006 Chiang Mai)

385
00:26:58,800 --> 00:26:59,880
Let me go!

386
00:27:00,950 --> 00:27:01,950
You bastard!

387
00:27:02,100 --> 00:27:03,080
Mungkorn.

388
00:27:11,270 --> 00:27:12,170
Help!

389
00:27:22,850 --> 00:27:24,000
Help me!

390
00:27:28,800 --> 00:27:29,820
Thear!

391
00:27:31,440 --> 00:27:32,420
Are you okay?

392
00:27:33,030 --> 00:27:34,040
I'm fine.

393
00:27:34,790 --> 00:27:35,850
You sure you're alright?

394
00:27:35,940 --> 00:27:36,690
Alright.

395
00:27:36,710 --> 00:27:37,680
Don't be afraid.

396
00:27:42,760 --> 00:27:44,360
I'll take care of every single
one of these bastards.

397
00:27:47,640 --> 00:27:48,820
Thear, look out!

398
00:28:01,580 --> 00:28:03,030
What a weak-ass kick.

399
00:28:13,800 --> 00:28:14,720
Come on! Bring it!

400
00:28:20,310 --> 00:28:21,240
Stop!

401
00:28:24,700 --> 00:28:25,630
What did you say?

402
00:28:26,600 --> 00:28:27,800
Enough already.

403
00:28:28,430 --> 00:28:29,560
Let's just talk this out.

404
00:28:31,350 --> 00:28:32,210
Enough?

405
00:28:33,170 --> 00:28:34,250
Like hell it is!

406
00:28:37,460 --> 00:28:38,150
No!

407
00:28:55,970 --> 00:28:56,750
Get over here.

408
00:28:58,440 --> 00:28:59,640
Stop it, Saming.

409
00:29:00,490 --> 00:29:01,640
That's enough!

410
00:29:15,680 --> 00:29:16,590
Thear!

411
00:29:16,900 --> 00:29:17,850
Thear!

412
00:29:33,680 --> 00:29:36,070
Well, look at you, Inspector Thear.

413
00:29:36,890 --> 00:29:38,990
You couldn't even put me behind bars.

414
00:29:41,180 --> 00:29:43,730
What the hell do you think
you can do to me? Huh?

415
00:29:44,510 --> 00:29:45,980
I'm begging you, Saming.

416
00:29:46,700 --> 00:29:47,970
Just let Mungkorn go.

417
00:29:49,780 --> 00:29:51,820
And settle this with me instead.

418
00:29:52,540 --> 00:29:54,610
Is playing the self-sacrificing saint

419
00:29:55,290 --> 00:29:57,560
why Mungkorn is so
head over heels for you?

420
00:29:59,690 --> 00:30:00,760
Is it, Mungkorn?

421
00:30:01,650 --> 00:30:03,260
I can also take care of you.

422
00:30:04,260 --> 00:30:06,380
Why don't you love me instead? Huh?

423
00:30:06,550 --> 00:30:08,330
Because I know who you really are.

424
00:30:08,950 --> 00:30:10,320
You're just a total fraud.

425
00:30:12,440 --> 00:30:14,030
But Inspector Thear is sincere.

426
00:30:14,740 --> 00:30:16,530
I love him without
needing any black magic.

427
00:30:17,430 --> 00:30:18,250
You...

428
00:30:19,150 --> 00:30:20,770
could never even come close to him.

429
00:30:22,250 --> 00:30:23,140
Good.

430
00:30:24,220 --> 00:30:25,450
Praise each other all you want.

431
00:30:25,980 --> 00:30:28,520
Let's see just how deep
your love really goes.

432
00:30:31,910 --> 00:30:33,260
I'll give you a choice.

433
00:30:35,100 --> 00:30:36,460
Between him...

434
00:30:43,120 --> 00:30:44,240
and your mother.

435
00:30:47,830 --> 00:30:49,810
I already have men
watching her in Phayao.

436
00:31:01,900 --> 00:31:02,720
Choose.

437
00:31:04,540 --> 00:31:06,500
Don't you dare lay
a finger on my mother!

438
00:31:07,490 --> 00:31:10,050
Well, that's entirely up to you.

439
00:31:10,690 --> 00:31:13,230
You can't have it all.

440
00:31:13,810 --> 00:31:15,830
If there's a wedding...

441
00:31:16,310 --> 00:31:17,880
there must be a funeral.

442
00:31:21,330 --> 00:31:22,160
Choose!

443
00:31:23,780 --> 00:31:25,000
Please...

444
00:31:26,110 --> 00:31:27,800
Let my mother and Inspector Thear go.

445
00:31:28,540 --> 00:31:30,240
I'll do anything you want.

446
00:31:33,490 --> 00:31:35,500
I'll do anything for you.

447
00:31:36,280 --> 00:31:38,810
I'll even marry you
if that's what you want.

448
00:31:38,850 --> 00:31:40,110
No, Mungkorn!

449
00:31:40,860 --> 00:31:43,280
I won't let you end up
with a piece of sh*t like him.

450
00:31:43,340 --> 00:31:44,560
Shut the hell up!

451
00:31:44,900 --> 00:31:45,950
Time's up.

452
00:31:47,660 --> 00:31:48,870
It's simple.

453
00:31:51,390 --> 00:31:52,270
Just choose!

454
00:31:59,160 --> 00:32:00,060
Mungkorn.

455
00:32:01,590 --> 00:32:05,930
Your mother is
the most important person in your life.

456
00:32:07,260 --> 00:32:08,630
Don't worry about me.

457
00:32:10,400 --> 00:32:12,830
During the months
we've spent together...

458
00:32:13,670 --> 00:32:15,620
I've been truly happy.

459
00:32:16,840 --> 00:32:19,540
But from now on,
stop doing things for me.

460
00:32:21,590 --> 00:32:23,530
Live your life for yourself.

461
00:32:24,750 --> 00:32:25,420
Okay?

462
00:32:26,460 --> 00:32:29,070
But you're
an important person in my life, too.

463
00:32:46,600 --> 00:32:48,760
Stop! Don't you dare come any closer!

464
00:32:49,990 --> 00:32:51,720
Get together! All of you, go!

465
00:32:52,020 --> 00:32:53,190
Don't come in!

466
00:32:54,290 --> 00:32:56,060
Or I'll blow his brains out.

467
00:32:56,190 --> 00:32:57,640
Untie Mungkorn right now!

468
00:32:58,270 --> 00:33:00,250
Tell your men to do it, goddammit!

469
00:33:01,310 --> 00:33:02,360
Untie him.

470
00:33:11,660 --> 00:33:12,550
No!

471
00:33:14,250 --> 00:33:14,850
Go!

472
00:33:16,230 --> 00:33:17,150
Go, Mungkorn!

473
00:33:20,130 --> 00:33:21,090
After them!

474
00:34:29,690 --> 00:34:30,500
Thear!

475
00:34:43,180 --> 00:34:44,440
Just come out.

476
00:34:45,930 --> 00:34:47,520
I've got this whole place shut down.

477
00:34:49,960 --> 00:34:51,900
You've got nowhere to run.

478
00:34:53,330 --> 00:34:54,320
This time...

479
00:34:54,870 --> 00:34:56,940
I'm not giving you a choice anymore.

480
00:34:58,230 --> 00:35:00,620
I'll let you both die together.

481
00:35:02,310 --> 00:35:03,200
Huh?

482
00:35:05,460 --> 00:35:07,130
It's pretty romantic, actually.

483
00:35:11,100 --> 00:35:13,940
A wedding and a funeral
just a few months apart.

484
00:35:15,910 --> 00:35:16,630
Huh?

485
00:35:18,530 --> 00:35:19,460
Come out!

486
00:35:23,350 --> 00:35:24,260
Thear.

487
00:35:24,410 --> 00:35:25,510
Thear.

488
00:35:26,470 --> 00:35:28,740
You're not actually any better than me.

489
00:35:30,160 --> 00:35:31,610
You're just lucky.

490
00:35:33,650 --> 00:35:34,740
Mungkorn.

491
00:35:36,020 --> 00:35:39,740
Choosing the wrong man
will haunt you for life.

492
00:35:50,140 --> 00:35:52,050
Hey, keep quiet.

493
00:37:19,460 --> 00:37:20,460
I told you.

494
00:37:21,630 --> 00:37:23,330
You'll never beat me.

495
00:37:56,100 --> 00:37:58,430
Saming, you're not
getting away this time.

496
00:37:58,650 --> 00:38:00,330
You've just earned yourself
even more charges.

497
00:38:00,610 --> 00:38:01,630
Hands up!

498
00:38:08,060 --> 00:38:09,110
Do it!

499
00:38:12,570 --> 00:38:14,010
Do you want to know why?

500
00:38:14,790 --> 00:38:16,290
It's because I have friends.

501
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:17,400
That's why I won.

502
00:38:31,280 --> 00:38:32,040
Come here.

503
00:38:37,100 --> 00:38:37,920
Mungkorn.

504
00:38:39,330 --> 00:38:40,430
Mungkorn, how are you?

505
00:38:40,830 --> 00:38:41,760
I'm fine.

506
00:38:43,460 --> 00:38:44,530
My mom.

507
00:38:46,490 --> 00:38:47,380
My mom...

508
00:38:49,670 --> 00:38:51,350
It's okay, Mungkorn. It's okay.

509
00:38:51,500 --> 00:38:53,010
Your mom will be safe.

510
00:39:09,850 --> 00:39:10,900
The wound is quite deep.

511
00:39:10,930 --> 00:39:13,510
I'll give you
some basic first aid for now.

512
00:39:13,540 --> 00:39:16,030
But you'll need to go to
the hospital for an X-ray later.

513
00:39:16,700 --> 00:39:18,140
Is it really that bad?

514
00:39:18,850 --> 00:39:20,820
Will I still be able to use my hand?

515
00:39:22,200 --> 00:39:23,710
It shouldn't be too serious.

516
00:39:24,200 --> 00:39:26,260
You survived getting shot
last time, didn't you?

517
00:39:26,600 --> 00:39:28,180
A hand injury is nothing next to that.

518
00:39:31,170 --> 00:39:33,410
As for the paperwork,
I can take care of it for you.

519
00:39:33,610 --> 00:39:34,710
You can just hand it over to me.

520
00:39:37,500 --> 00:39:38,780
It's my dominant hand, too.

521
00:39:39,620 --> 00:39:40,830
I can't do anything at all.

522
00:39:43,750 --> 00:39:45,650
It doesn't matter
if you can't do anything.

523
00:39:45,870 --> 00:39:47,700
You have a husband to do
everything for you now.

524
00:39:52,060 --> 00:39:53,990
And don't worry about your mom.

525
00:39:54,540 --> 00:39:56,140
Inspector Thear is handling it.

526
00:40:00,030 --> 00:40:01,810
Everything's clear on
the Phayao side, right?

527
00:40:02,980 --> 00:40:03,750
Is that so?

528
00:40:03,790 --> 00:40:04,790
It's all settled?

529
00:40:06,340 --> 00:40:07,400
Okay, alright.

530
00:40:08,040 --> 00:40:09,140
Thank you so much.

531
00:40:09,960 --> 00:40:11,390
I'll find a way to repay you.

532
00:40:20,200 --> 00:40:21,820
I've already handed Saming over.

533
00:40:21,970 --> 00:40:23,660
He's definitely not
getting away this time.

534
00:40:25,290 --> 00:40:26,930
No higher-ups are going to stick
their necks out for him.

535
00:40:26,950 --> 00:40:28,300
They wouldn't want to
get dragged down with him.

536
00:40:33,010 --> 00:40:35,580
When is this string of bad luck
ever going to end for you and Mungkorn?

537
00:40:36,040 --> 00:40:37,410
It's just one disaster after another.

538
00:40:37,980 --> 00:40:40,860
If I hadn't been tracking the GPS on
Saming's car since last time,

539
00:40:40,890 --> 00:40:42,390
I might not have made it
in time to help you.

540
00:40:43,320 --> 00:40:45,390
Why didn't you tell your friends
what you were planning to do?

541
00:40:47,170 --> 00:40:49,160
I don't think this has anything
to do with bad luck anymore.

542
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:51,960
This was all just Saming being
a complete piece of sh*t.

543
00:40:55,480 --> 00:40:56,640
Honestly, though...

544
00:40:57,870 --> 00:41:00,060
with all these terrible things,

545
00:41:00,660 --> 00:41:02,100
I'm starting to have my doubts.

546
00:41:04,670 --> 00:41:08,210
What if Mungkorn and I just aren't
meant for each other after all?

547
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:11,090
Thear.

548
00:41:12,560 --> 00:41:14,000
I received the report.

549
00:41:14,180 --> 00:41:14,960
I was worried.

550
00:41:15,450 --> 00:41:16,400
How are you doing?

551
00:41:19,740 --> 00:41:21,690
I'm okay, Dad. It's nothing serious.

552
00:41:22,890 --> 00:41:25,050
And Mungkorn? Is he alright?

553
00:41:39,740 --> 00:41:41,190
He got a bit banged up, Dad.

554
00:41:45,180 --> 00:41:46,200
Well, that's good then.

555
00:41:48,290 --> 00:41:51,740
Your mother's plan to ward off
bad luck by getting you married...

556
00:41:53,240 --> 00:41:55,240
I don't think it worked at all.

557
00:42:13,470 --> 00:42:14,220
Dad.

558
00:42:17,360 --> 00:42:18,660
I have a favor to ask.

559
00:42:24,380 --> 00:42:25,680
I think it's finally time

560
00:42:26,900 --> 00:42:29,440
for me to fulfill the promise
I made to Mungkorn.

561
00:42:33,180 --> 00:42:34,290
What promise?

562
00:42:45,100 --> 00:42:46,850
- Here, let me light it for you.
- Okay.

563
00:42:46,870 --> 00:42:47,800
Thank you.

564
00:42:48,500 --> 00:42:50,430
My hand is totally out of commission.

565
00:42:55,330 --> 00:42:57,590
When can you take these bandages off?

566
00:42:59,230 --> 00:43:00,470
In just a few days.

567
00:43:00,530 --> 00:43:02,480
It'll be back to normal in no time.

568
00:43:07,350 --> 00:43:08,800
What's with the sudden mood?

569
00:43:09,120 --> 00:43:10,680
Suddenly wanting to come and pray.

570
00:43:13,700 --> 00:43:15,160
We've been through so much together.

571
00:43:16,510 --> 00:43:19,580
I just wanted to come and pray
for some good fortune in our lives.

572
00:43:21,960 --> 00:43:23,570
It's fitting for a fresh start.

573
00:43:23,600 --> 00:43:24,720
Doesn't hurt to do it, right?

574
00:43:34,620 --> 00:43:36,770
Now, repeat after me.

575
00:43:38,370 --> 00:43:39,170
Okay.

576
00:43:43,340 --> 00:43:44,300
"I am..."

577
00:43:45,400 --> 00:43:46,560
I am...

578
00:43:48,160 --> 00:43:49,760
"Mr. Mungkorn Phianwanich..."

579
00:43:51,710 --> 00:43:53,640
Mr. Mungkorn Phianwanich...

580
00:43:56,080 --> 00:43:59,340
"I hereby revoke my soul-binding oath

581
00:43:59,700 --> 00:44:01,790
with Mr. Theartha Phiromsamorn

582
00:44:02,470 --> 00:44:04,010
from this moment onward."

583
00:44:11,860 --> 00:44:14,520
"May all bonds come to an end.

584
00:44:14,830 --> 00:44:16,570
May both of us be set free.

585
00:44:17,150 --> 00:44:18,690
Each following their own karma,

586
00:44:19,090 --> 00:44:21,230
no longer affecting one another."

587
00:44:23,320 --> 00:44:24,820
What is the meaning of this?

588
00:44:33,430 --> 00:44:35,170
I think we should get a divorce.

589
00:44:54,400 --> 00:44:57,260
I've already had my father arrange
your transfer to Phayao.

590
00:44:58,210 --> 00:45:01,010
From now on,
there's nothing left between us.

591
00:45:14,140 --> 00:45:16,060
(Subject: Transfer of a Civil Servant)

592
00:45:16,090 --> 00:45:17,660
(To: Police Senior Sergeant Major
Mungkorn Phianwanich)

593
00:45:18,040 --> 00:45:20,030
You planned every single thing...

594
00:45:21,640 --> 00:45:24,280
without ever thinking to talk to me?
Not even a word?

595
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:27,100
I used to think...

596
00:45:28,190 --> 00:45:29,890
that our love...

597
00:45:30,410 --> 00:45:33,010
would carry us
through all this mess.

598
00:45:34,660 --> 00:45:35,760
But I was wrong.

599
00:45:38,220 --> 00:45:40,320
No one can defy destiny.

600
00:45:42,100 --> 00:45:45,800
I can't bear to see you get hurt
because of me anymore.

601
00:45:55,800 --> 00:45:57,900
But is there really no other way?

602
00:46:00,640 --> 00:46:03,490
Didn't we promise that
no matter what happened...

603
00:46:04,080 --> 00:46:06,480
we'd face it together?

604
00:46:23,340 --> 00:46:25,840
Since you've already made
the decision yourself, Inspector...

605
00:46:41,720 --> 00:46:42,640
I am...

606
00:46:43,710 --> 00:46:45,570
Mr. Mungkorn Phianwanich.

607
00:46:47,790 --> 00:46:51,700
I hereby revoke my soul-binding oath...

608
00:46:53,720 --> 00:46:55,770
with Mr. Theartha Phiromsamorn

609
00:46:56,740 --> 00:46:58,440
from this moment onward.

610
00:47:01,690 --> 00:47:04,100
May all bonds come to an end.

611
00:47:05,670 --> 00:47:07,590
May both of us be set free.

612
00:47:08,410 --> 00:47:09,720
Each following their own karma,

613
00:47:11,520 --> 00:47:13,390
no longer affecting one another.

614
00:48:27,540 --> 00:48:29,240
Are you sure about this, Thear?

615
00:48:31,950 --> 00:48:32,660
Yes, Mom.

616
00:48:38,200 --> 00:48:40,400
The first time I met Mungkorn,

617
00:48:40,420 --> 00:48:43,720
I knew there was something
very special between you two.

618
00:48:44,420 --> 00:48:45,780
Won't you reconsider?

619
00:48:46,410 --> 00:48:48,420
You two have been
through so much together.

620
00:48:49,670 --> 00:48:50,470
Thear...

621
00:48:51,300 --> 00:48:52,990
We could find another way, son.

622
00:49:02,610 --> 00:49:04,310
Please don't try to stop
Inspector Thear.

623
00:49:06,100 --> 00:49:07,570
I'm sure he's thought this through.

624
00:49:12,940 --> 00:49:14,700
If he believes this is the way out,

625
00:49:16,560 --> 00:49:18,740
we have to respect his decision.

626
00:49:21,560 --> 00:49:22,820
My life...

627
00:49:26,910 --> 00:49:27,700
has belonged to him

628
00:49:27,730 --> 00:49:29,590
ever since I agreed to sign
that marriage certificate.

629
00:49:45,010 --> 00:49:46,310
(Mr. Theartha Phiromsamorn,
Thai, 35 years old)

630
00:49:46,330 --> 00:49:47,560
(Mr. Mungkorn Phianwanich,
Thai, 28 years old)

631
00:50:21,190 --> 00:50:24,370
(Chiang Mai Municipality)

632
00:50:32,840 --> 00:50:34,700
You can just
drop me off here, Inspector.

633
00:50:35,910 --> 00:50:37,140
I'll take care of the rest myself.

634
00:50:42,660 --> 00:50:44,610
I could drive you all the way home.

635
00:50:48,150 --> 00:50:49,410
It's better if you don't.

636
00:50:51,060 --> 00:50:52,830
Please, no more kindness.

637
00:50:54,970 --> 00:50:57,100
That way, neither of us owes
the other anything.

638
00:51:10,280 --> 00:51:11,050
Here.

639
00:51:11,940 --> 00:51:13,780
A million-baht check, as promised.

640
00:51:17,200 --> 00:51:18,560
Take good care of yourself.

641
00:51:25,560 --> 00:51:27,600
I want to thank you for everything.

642
00:51:30,460 --> 00:51:31,620
About the house...

643
00:51:32,540 --> 00:51:35,460
if you run into any trouble,
just let me know.

644
00:51:35,570 --> 00:51:36,590
I'll help you out myself.

645
00:51:44,280 --> 00:51:46,280
I'd rather not accept this.

646
00:51:52,180 --> 00:51:53,690
With a civil servant's salary like mine,

647
00:51:54,860 --> 00:51:56,410
I should be able to get a loan anyway.

648
00:51:57,800 --> 00:51:59,310
I don't need to depend on you.

649
00:52:00,620 --> 00:52:01,340
But...

650
00:52:01,820 --> 00:52:03,740
But this is what you deserve.

651
00:52:04,900 --> 00:52:06,620
For all the time you've lost.

652
00:52:13,530 --> 00:52:15,220
I'll consider it a life lesson.

653
00:52:17,750 --> 00:52:19,840
It's worth far more than this check.

654
00:52:34,480 --> 00:52:35,790
I have to go now.

655
00:52:38,560 --> 00:52:40,160
Thank you for everything.

656
00:52:59,390 --> 00:53:00,280
Inspector.

657
00:53:05,580 --> 00:53:07,380
I hope you stay safe,

658
00:53:08,710 --> 00:53:10,250
now and forever.

659
00:53:22,550 --> 00:53:26,410
♪I'm sorry for hurting you♪

660
00:53:27,710 --> 00:53:31,530
♪And all the pain I've put you through♪

661
00:53:31,900 --> 00:53:36,390
♪But I can't turn back time♪

662
00:53:36,680 --> 00:53:42,590
♪To make things right♪

663
00:53:44,590 --> 00:53:47,990
♪I'm sorry I was blind♪

664
00:53:48,020 --> 00:53:52,850
♪To the tears behind your eyes♪

665
00:53:53,610 --> 00:53:57,970
♪They're the clearest evidence♪

666
00:53:58,000 --> 00:54:03,950
♪That I've been so heartless♪

667
00:54:05,630 --> 00:54:10,790
♪The only way to stop your pain♪

668
00:54:11,120 --> 00:54:16,340
♪Is to leave and not return again♪

669
00:54:16,700 --> 00:54:21,460
♪Despite our love,
I need this to be over♪

670
00:54:21,490 --> 00:54:27,180
♪I can't watch you suffer any longer♪

671
00:54:28,050 --> 00:54:33,270
♪I'm the one who deserves to cry♪

672
00:54:33,290 --> 00:54:37,040
♪I've lost the right
to have you by my side♪

673
00:54:37,070 --> 00:54:40,080
♪I'm letting go of your hand♪

674
00:54:41,400 --> 00:54:43,280
I'm begging you.
Please tell me how to fix this.

675
00:54:44,360 --> 00:54:47,830
Mungkorn shall take your misfortune
upon himself

676
00:54:48,750 --> 00:54:54,390
until the day one of you
betrays the vows or ends the marriage.

677
00:54:54,820 --> 00:54:57,720
Another way lies in divorce.

678
00:54:58,050 --> 00:54:59,050
When that time comes,

679
00:54:59,590 --> 00:55:04,190
the scales of fate will gradually return
to their former balance.

680
00:55:04,690 --> 00:55:10,180
♪The only way to stop your pain♪

681
00:55:10,210 --> 00:55:15,720
♪Is to leave and not return again♪

682
00:55:15,750 --> 00:55:20,250
♪Despite our love,
I need this to be over♪

683
00:55:20,490 --> 00:55:26,350
♪I can't watch you suffer any longer♪

684
00:55:27,060 --> 00:55:32,240
♪I'm the one who deserves to cry♪

685
00:55:32,270 --> 00:55:36,020
♪I've lost the right
to have you by my side♪

686
00:55:36,050 --> 00:55:39,080
♪I'm letting go of your hand♪

687
00:55:39,100 --> 00:55:44,520
♪The more I hold on,
the more selfish I am♪

688
00:55:44,540 --> 00:55:48,450
♪Don't you agree?♪

689
00:55:49,110 --> 00:55:54,350
♪I'm the one who should be crying♪

690
00:55:54,370 --> 00:55:58,120
♪I'll gladly say goodbye,
though inside I'm dying♪

691
00:55:58,140 --> 00:56:01,220
♪Our time has finally run out♪

692
00:56:01,250 --> 00:56:07,090
♪It's only right that I must leave♪

693
00:56:07,400 --> 00:56:12,940
♪Let me be the one to grieve♪

694
00:56:33,260 --> 00:56:38,500
♪I'm the one who should be crying♪

695
00:56:38,520 --> 00:56:42,270
♪I'll gladly say goodbye,
though inside I'm dying♪

696
00:56:42,290 --> 00:56:45,370
♪Our time has finally run out♪

697
00:56:45,400 --> 00:56:51,240
♪It's only right that I must leave♪

698
00:56:51,550 --> 00:56:56,650
♪Let me be the one to grieve♪

699
00:57:02,320 --> 00:57:04,290
If you really want Mungkorn back,

700
00:57:04,310 --> 00:57:06,970
you need to show him
that you mean it this time.

701
00:57:06,990 --> 00:57:07,900
Go away!

702
00:57:08,120 --> 00:57:08,870
No.

703
00:57:08,900 --> 00:57:10,290
Not until you forgive me.

704
00:57:11,220 --> 00:57:11,900
Mungkorn...

705
00:57:11,930 --> 00:57:12,940
Do you find it that easy

706
00:57:12,970 --> 00:57:15,490
to keep changing
what we are to each other?

707
00:57:15,580 --> 00:57:17,710
If you can't take it anymore,
then forgive me.

708
00:57:17,860 --> 00:57:20,190
Can't you give us another chance?

709
00:57:20,610 --> 00:57:21,410
I...
